{"name":"Raven Grey","hex":"#6f747b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several, generally large, species of birds in the genus Corvus with lustrous black plumage; especially the common raven (Corvus corax).","A jet-black, often glossy, colour, like that of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the jet-black and often glossy colour of the plumage of a raven (etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raven"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raven","blocks":[{"text":"A raven is any of several large-bodied passerine bird species in the genus Corvus. These species do not form a single taxonomic group within the genus. There is no consistent distinction between crows and ravens; the two names are assigned to different species mainly by size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/3782_Common_Raven_in_flight.jpg/330px-3782_Common_Raven_in_flight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raven"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://